  "comment": "The golden demo requests. Both contract guards replay this list: api/tests/test_contract_snapshot.py (backend) and frontend/tests/contract.golden.test.ts (frontend). 'path' is the concrete request path without the /api/v1 prefix. '__FIRST_FILE__' means: take the first file_id from GET /files on your own side. 'openapi_path' is the matching path template in api/docs/openapi.v1.json. 'query' values may be strings or arrays of strings — array values become repeated query params (contract §E4, multi-value filters), replayed by URLSearchParams.append on the FE and by passing lists to httpx.params on the BE. Edit this file only together with plans/API-CONTRACT.md and the snapshot, in one commit. Golden 22-24 cover the table-filters slice (multi-value status, size_bytes sort, missing_unit quick view). Golden 25 covers the Explore tab context; its 404 run_not_found path is an error status with no per-route body schema in the snapshot, so — like the 422 case below — it is not carried here and its behavioral coverage lives in api/tests/test_explore_routes.py. Golden 26 (the scoped explore query) was removed on 24 Aug 2026 with POST /explore/query: the workbench posts its SQL straight to QuixLake through the frontend (plans/design/EXPLORE-DIRECT-LAKE.md). Golden 28 and 29 cover the two FR-DM-111 catalogue filters added 24 Aug 2026, dtype and source_system; golden 14b already replays GET /signals/facets, so the two new facet lists ride that entry. Golden 30 and 31 cover FR-DM-108, added 24 Aug 2026: the grouped runs route (contract §2c) and the test_cell filter on the flat list. The 422 for a bad group_by is a per-field case, so it stays in api/tests/test_runs_grouping.py with the other 422 cases. 422 goldens are not carried yet. The reason changed on 21 Aug 2026: the snapshot now carries the real 422 body (ValidationErrorResponse: {detail, code, errors}), so the old reason is dead. What remains is that a golden replays one request and asserts one status, and the 